1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,216
A rock by a country road.

2
00:00:02,216 --> 00:00:04,428
The bark of a tree in the hills.

3
00:00:04,428 --> 00:00:06,099
A wall in a smoky city.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,454
The first two are covered
in grey-green patches.

5
00:00:09,454 --> 00:00:11,085
The city wall has none.

6
00:00:11,085 --> 00:00:11,985
Why?

7
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:16,280
Aarav rides past those patches
on his bicycle road every day.

8
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,987
Diya told him: that patch
is not one living thing.

9
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:20,986
It is two.

10
00:00:21,336 --> 00:00:25,461
By the end, you will know who the two
partners are, what each one gives,

11
00:00:25,461 --> 00:00:27,868
and why the patches vanish from dirty air.

12
00:00:28,518 --> 00:00:29,904
So what is that patch?

13
00:00:30,254 --> 00:00:31,553
It is a lichen.

14
00:00:31,553 --> 00:00:36,539
A lichen is a symbiotic association:
two different organisms living together,

15
00:00:36,539 --> 00:00:38,268
and both of them gain.

16
00:00:38,718 --> 00:00:41,520
The two partners are an alga and a fungus.

17
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:44,527
The alga is called the phycobiont.

18
00:00:44,527 --> 00:00:45,943
Phyco means alga.

19
00:00:45,943 --> 00:00:48,555
The fungus is called the mycobiont.

20
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:50,027
Myco means fungus.

21
00:00:50,677 --> 00:00:54,872
Now let's zoom into the patch on
Aarav's rock, one level at a time.

22
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:59,499
On the rock, the lichen is a flat,
crusty patch, firmly stuck down.

23
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:00,899
Zoom in.

24
00:01:00,794 --> 00:01:03,333
The patch has wavy, leaf-like lobes.

25
00:01:03,333 --> 00:01:06,161
Most of its body is made by the fungus.

26
00:01:06,661 --> 00:01:07,587
Zoom again.

27
00:01:07,587 --> 00:01:08,935
Cut a thin slice.

28
00:01:08,935 --> 00:01:12,961
Packed fungal threads, the
hyphae, form the top and bottom.

29
00:01:12,961 --> 00:01:16,332
In between lies a thin
green layer of algal cells.

30
00:01:16,832 --> 00:01:18,585
Zoom into one algal cell.

31
00:01:18,585 --> 00:01:20,981
Fungal hyphae wrap tightly around it.

32
00:01:20,981 --> 00:01:23,435
This is where the two partners trade.

33
00:01:24,085 --> 00:01:26,725
Let's follow that trade,
one step at a time.

34
00:01:27,075 --> 00:01:27,975
Step one.

35
00:01:27,925 --> 00:01:29,728
The alga has chlorophyll.

36
00:01:29,728 --> 00:01:31,957
Using sunlight, it makes food.

37
00:01:31,957 --> 00:01:35,532
So the alga is autotrophic:
it makes its own food.

38
00:01:36,282 --> 00:01:37,182
Step two.

39
00:01:37,121 --> 00:01:40,446
The alga passes some of
that food to the fungus.

40
00:01:40,446 --> 00:01:42,543
The fungus has no chlorophyll.

41
00:01:42,543 --> 00:01:45,847
It is heterotrophic: it
needs food from outside.

42
00:01:46,597 --> 00:01:47,525
Step three.

43
00:01:47,525 --> 00:01:50,278
The fungus wraps the alga in its hyphae.

44
00:01:50,278 --> 00:01:52,244
That gives the alga shelter.

45
00:01:52,994 --> 00:01:53,902
Step four.

46
00:01:53,902 --> 00:01:58,514
The fungus also absorbs water and
mineral nutrients, and passes them to

47
00:01:58,514 --> 00:01:59,414
the alga.

48
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:01,019
Step five.

49
00:02:00,944 --> 00:02:05,237
The partnership is so close that,
looking at a lichen, you would never

50
00:02:05,237 --> 00:02:06,991
guess it is two organisms.

51
00:02:07,741 --> 00:02:09,525
Now back to the smoky city.

52
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:12,838
Lichens are very good
pollution indicators.

53
00:02:12,838 --> 00:02:15,435
They do not grow in polluted areas.

54
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:19,697
So when lichens grow well on
rocks and trees, the air is clean.

55
00:02:19,697 --> 00:02:22,074
When they disappear, the air is dirty.

56
00:02:22,074 --> 00:02:24,283
That is why the city wall had none.

57
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:28,728
A lichen is one kind of
relationship between two species.

58
00:02:28,728 --> 00:02:31,364
Let's compare three kinds side by side.

59
00:02:31,714 --> 00:02:33,973
Mutualism: both partners gain.

60
00:02:33,973 --> 00:02:35,973
The lichen is one example.

61
00:02:35,973 --> 00:02:40,632
Another is mycorrhiza: a fungus on
plant roots absorbs phosphorus from

62
00:02:40,632 --> 00:02:44,697
the soil for the plant, and
the plant feeds the fungus.

63
00:02:45,147 --> 00:02:49,845
Commensalism: one partner gains, and
the other neither gains nor loses.

64
00:02:49,845 --> 00:02:53,222
An orchid growing on a
mango branch is an example.

65
00:02:53,672 --> 00:02:57,340
Parasitism: one partner gains,
and the other is harmed.

66
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:00,625
The fungus Albugo on a
mustard leaf is an example.

67
00:03:01,275 --> 00:03:02,234
Your turn.

68
00:03:02,234 --> 00:03:06,993
A cattle egret walks beside grazing
cattle and catches the insects they

69
00:03:06,993 --> 00:03:07,893
stir up.

70
00:03:07,842 --> 00:03:09,990
The cattle are not affected.

71
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:11,896
Mutualism or commensalism?

72
00:03:11,896 --> 00:03:13,306
Pause and decide.

73
00:03:16,506 --> 00:03:17,506
Commensalism!

74
00:03:17,506 --> 00:03:21,630
The egret gains food, and the
cattle neither gain nor lose.

75
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,362
Remember this.

76
00:03:23,362 --> 00:03:27,791
A lichen is two organisms, an
alga and a fungus, living as one.

77
00:03:28,391 --> 00:03:29,927
Now a worked example.

78
00:03:29,927 --> 00:03:33,100
Let's sort five partnerships
into the three kinds.

79
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:37,837
A lichen: the alga gives food, the
fungus gives shelter and water.

80
00:03:37,837 --> 00:03:40,006
Both gain, so it is mutualism.

81
00:03:40,456 --> 00:03:44,727
Mycorrhiza: the plant gets
phosphorus, the fungus gets food.

82
00:03:44,727 --> 00:03:45,979
Mutualism again.

83
00:03:46,429 --> 00:03:51,559
An orchid on a mango branch: the orchid
gains, the mango tree is not affected.

84
00:03:51,559 --> 00:03:52,497
Commensalism.

85
00:03:52,947 --> 00:03:56,918
Albugo on mustard: the fungus
feeds, and the leaf is harmed.

86
00:03:56,918 --> 00:03:57,818
Parasitism.

87
00:03:57,748 --> 00:04:00,618
And the egret with the
cattle: commensalism.

88
00:04:01,268 --> 00:04:02,733
Now, the exam trap.

89
00:04:03,083 --> 00:04:06,859
Many students write that in a
lichen, the fungus makes the food.

90
00:04:07,259 --> 00:04:09,547
But only the alga has chlorophyll.

91
00:04:09,547 --> 00:04:11,578
The phycobiont makes the food.

92
00:04:11,578 --> 00:04:14,719
The mycobiont gives
shelter, water and minerals.

93
00:04:15,369 --> 00:04:16,840
Where is this asked?

94
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:21,083
As one-line statements: which partner
is autotrophic, and what lichens

95
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,712
tell us about the air.

96
00:04:23,312 --> 00:04:24,539
Exam level now.

97
00:04:24,539 --> 00:04:26,941
Read the assertion and the reason.

98
00:04:26,941 --> 00:04:28,698
Choose the right option.

99
00:04:28,698 --> 00:04:29,977
Pause and solve.

100
00:04:35,377 --> 00:04:36,646
The answer is C.

101
00:04:37,146 --> 00:04:38,848
The assertion is true.

102
00:04:38,848 --> 00:04:43,408
Lichens are pollution indicators
and do not grow in polluted areas.

103
00:04:43,908 --> 00:04:45,477
The reason is false.

104
00:04:45,477 --> 00:04:50,510
It is the other way round: the phycobiont
is autotrophic, and the mycobiont

105
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:51,795
is heterotrophic.

106
00:04:52,395 --> 00:04:53,859
Here is your recap.

107
00:04:53,859 --> 00:04:55,363
Screenshot this card.

108
00:04:58,563 --> 00:05:01,400
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

109
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:02,700
One.

110
00:05:02,247 --> 00:05:05,182
What does each partner
give the other in a lichen?

111
00:05:06,082 --> 00:05:06,982
Two.

112
00:05:06,649 --> 00:05:09,827
How is commensalism
different from mutualism?

113
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:11,627
Three.

114
00:05:11,323 --> 00:05:13,894
Why can lichens tell us about the air?

115
00:05:14,994 --> 00:05:18,024
Next time: a cold that
no antibiotic can cure.

116
00:05:18,024 --> 00:05:19,781
What is really causing it?

117
00:05:19,781 --> 00:05:22,515
We find out in viruses
and their structure.
